        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72159?u=f25bf9f675b806b92a8e5083ce5d0b8f1d7708df&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">RFC for the issue <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"654099587\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/74182\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rust/issues/74182/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/74182\">rust-lang/rust#74182</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/kornelski/rfcs/blob/stable_since/text/0000-stable_since.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3854",
            "title": "RFC for `#[stable(since)]`",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-14T01:16:24.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-12T14:25:02.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "kornelski",
                "url": "https://github.com/kornelski"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6884440?u=cad7a9bd658ee65b0cebefb9421c21ef2cd4b66f&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">We would like to propose <code class=\"notranslate\">auto impl</code> syntax for supertraits for a few language enhancement, to ultimately facilitate easier trait evolution and refactoring and easier trait authoring when trait hierarchy is in consideration.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/dingxiangfei2009/rust-rfcs/blob/supertrait-auto-impls/text/0000-supertrait-auto-impls.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3851",
            "title": "Supertrait Auto-impl",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-30T15:12:51.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-26T12:05:15.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "dingxiangfei2009",
                "url": "https://github.com/dingxiangfei2009"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81586710?u=432678424793bd56d22e6932670f86934ff70e92&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h1 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h1>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This RFC introduces an attribute for marking files as autogenerated. This syntax can be used by everything from rustbindgen to protoc (protobuf compiler) and understood by humans and tools alike.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-rust notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"mod foo {\n\t#![autogenerated(\n\t\tby = &quot;example tool&quot;,\n\t\tsuppress_lints = false,\n\t\tformat = true,\n\t\tregen_hint = &quot;./regen_example_tool&quot;,\n\t\tdocument = false,\n\t\tstable_api = true,\n\t)]\n\t// autogenerated code here...\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">mod</span> foo <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span>\n\t<span class=\"pl-c1\">#!<span class=\"pl-kos\">[</span>autogenerated<span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span></span>\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">\t\tby = <span class=\"pl-s\">\"example tool\"</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">\t\tsuppress_lints = <span class=\"pl-c1\">false</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">\t\tformat = <span class=\"pl-c1\">true</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">\t\tregen_hint = <span class=\"pl-s\">\"./regen_example_tool\"</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">\t\tdocument = <span class=\"pl-c1\">false</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">\t\tstable_api = <span class=\"pl-c1\">true</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">\t<span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">]</span></span>\n\t<span class=\"pl-c\">// autogenerated code here...</span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Aversefun/rfcs/blob/master/text/3850-autogenerated-attr.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3850",
            "title": "RFC: Autogenerated Attribute",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-30T06:31:32.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-24T18:28:14.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Aversefun",
                "url": "https://github.com/Aversefun"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/928074?u=34b16e2e7d89c10be8992a845915ab8af13f5570&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">const</code> operand to <code class=\"notranslate\">asm!</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">global_asm!</code> currently only accepts integers. Change it to also accept pointer values. The value must be computed during const evaluation. The operand expands to the name of the symbol that the<br>\npointer references, plus an integer offset when necessary.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Darksonn/rfcs/blob/asm-const-ptr/text/3848-asm-const-ptr.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3848",
            "title": "Pass pointers to `const` in assembly",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-20T15:43:29.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-10T09:52:51.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Darksonn",
                "url": "https://github.com/Darksonn"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/79958059?u=d009ef52a27ec00bf252f237d133f451840a80e2&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Feature Name: Include Clang in llvm-tools</li>\n<li>Start Date: 2025-08-04</li>\n<li>RFC PR: <a href=\"\">rust-lang/rfcs#3847</a></li>\n<li>Rust Issue: <a href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/0000\">rust-lang/rust#0000</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h1 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h1>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Include a version of <code class=\"notranslate\">clang</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">clang++</code> compiled against Rust LLVM in the <code class=\"notranslate\">llvm-tools</code> component in nightly.</p>\n<h1 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h1>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Allowing user-access to the LLVM pipeline allows for many user-built features, such as cross-language inlining. However, LLVM version mismatching between tools can lead to frustrating problems. Including <code class=\"notranslate\">clang</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">clang++</code> in <code class=\"notranslate\">llvm-tools</code> allows users to use only the tools that Rust ships with, ensuring consistent versioning.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In future versions of Rust, including a compiler with Rustup could also improve ergonomics for FFI crates, as it could avoid depending on system compilers. See how <a href=\"https://actually.fyi/posts/zig-makes-rust-cross-compilation-just-work/\" rel=\"nofollow\">Zig's implementation</a> led to easy cross-compiles in rust to Macos.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Background</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">clang</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">clang++</code> are LLVM-based C and C++ compilers mentioned in <a href=\"https://doc.rust-lang.org/rustc/linker-plugin-lto.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">official documentation</a>:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"# Compile the Rust staticlib\nRUSTFLAGS=&quot;-Clinker-plugin-lto&quot; cargo build --release\n# Compile the C code with `-flto=thin`\nclang -c -O2 -flto=thin -o cmain.o ./cmain.c\n# Link everything, making sure that we use an appropriate linker\nclang -flto=thin -fuse-ld=lld -L . -l&quot;name-of-your-rust-lib&quot; -o main -O2 ./cmain.o\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> Compile the Rust staticlib</span>\nRUSTFLAGS=<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>-Clinker-plugin-lto<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span> cargo build --release\n<span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> Compile the C code with `-flto=thin`</span>\nclang -c -O2 -flto=thin -o cmain.o ./cmain.c\n<span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> Link everything, making sure that we use an appropriate linker</span>\nclang -flto=thin -fuse-ld=lld -L <span class=\"pl-c1\">.</span> -l<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>name-of-your-rust-lib<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span> -o main -O2 ./cmain.o</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Unfortunately, this example does not always work, because it calls system <code class=\"notranslate\">clang</code>, which may use a different version of LLVM than Rust. Additionally, even at the same version, there is a potential for problems from mixing base LLVM tools with the Rust fork of LLVM.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Rustup has the ability to install a component called <code class=\"notranslate\">llvm-tools</code>, which exposes the llvm tools used by Rust, including <code class=\"notranslate\">llvm-link</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">llc</code> - notably, it does not contain a build of <code class=\"notranslate\">clang</code> or <code class=\"notranslate\">clang++</code>.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Conclusion</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Builds of <code class=\"notranslate\">clang</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">clang++</code> should be added to the <code class=\"notranslate\">llvm-tools</code> component to enable version matching when working with base LLVM tools.</p>\n<h1 dir=\"auto\">Drawbacks</h1>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This will increase compile times and require more storage on devices with the <code class=\"notranslate\">llvm-tools</code> component installed.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It may also drive more people to use manual compilation processes, which may cause fragmentation or be at odds with the Rust vision.</p>\n<h1 dir=\"auto\">Rationale and alternatives</h1>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Users can opt for system <code class=\"notranslate\">clang</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">clang++</code> when building projects with LLVM, however there is no guarantee that users will have an appropriate version of the system tools, or that the Rust fork of LLVM won't contain any breaking changes.</p>\n<h1 dir=\"auto\">Prior art</h1>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This may help in the goal <a href=\"https://rust-lang.github.io/rust-project-goals/2025h1/GPU-Offload.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">Expose experimental LLVM features for GPU offloading</a>, as raw LLVM access is particularly useful for GPU compilation libraries.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This was mentioned in <a href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/56371\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rust/issues/56371/hovercard\">Shipping clang as a Rustup component</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See also the issues for <a href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/55890\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rust/issues/55890/hovercard\"><code class=\"notranslate\">llvm-dis</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">llc</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">opt</code></a></p>\n<h1 dir=\"auto\">Unresolved questions</h1>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Should <code class=\"notranslate\">clang</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">clang++</code> be part of the <code class=\"notranslate\">llvm-tools</code> component or added as their own component?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/SirAlienTheGreat/rfcs/blob/master/text/0000-include-clang-in-llvm-tools.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3847",
            "title": "Include Clang in llvm-tools",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-05T19:08:10.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-06T22:07:48.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "SirAlienTheGreat",
                "url": "https://github.com/SirAlienTheGreat"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16103364?u=09ef08026fda09489818ee682ecd4a8663e89af3&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Add <code class=\"notranslate\">repr(ordered_fields)</code> and provide a migration path to switch users from <code class=\"notranslate\">repr(C)</code> to <code class=\"notranslate\">repr(ordered_fields)</code>, then change the meaning of <code class=\"notranslate\">repr(C)</code> in the next edition.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This RFC is meant to be an MVP, and any extensions (for example, adding more <code class=\"notranslate\">repr</code>s) are not in scope. This is done to make it as easy as possible to accept this RFC and make progress on the issue of <code class=\"notranslate\">repr(C)</code> serving two opposing roles.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/RustyYato/rfcs/blob/repr_ordered_fields/text/3845-repr-ordered-fields.md\">Rendered</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">To avoid endless bikeshedding, I'll make a poll if this RFC is accepted with all the potential names for the new <code class=\"notranslate\">repr</code>. If you have a new name, I'll add it to the list of names in the unresolved questions section, and will include it in the poll.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3845",
            "title": "repr(ordered_fields)",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-10T06:05:37.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-05T16:01:05.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "RustyYato",
                "url": "https://github.com/RustyYato"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18526288?u=a851e2ec349404d3ad63a62786fe9a35009fa8d1&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Move to a world where the size check for <code class=\"notranslate\">transmute</code> is always accurate, preserving the developer experience via linting instead of the special-cased typeck tricks.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/scottmcm/rfcs/blob/newt_level_transfiguration/text/3844-next-gen-transmute.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3844",
            "title": "Next-Gen `transmute`",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-22T07:38:59.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-02T23:28:32.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "scottmcm",
                "url": "https://github.com/scottmcm"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25300418?u=cbf913d695b914864c7109773cacdd88ab7d96b1&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h1 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h1>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This RFC introduces a concise safety-comment convention for unsafe code in standard libraries:<br>\ntag every public unsafe function with <code class=\"notranslate\">#[safety::requires]</code> and call with <code class=\"notranslate\">#[safety::checked]</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Safety tags refine today’s safety-comment habits: a featherweight syntax that condenses every<br>\nrequirement into a single, check-off reminder.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The following snippet <a href=\"https://play.rust-lang.org/?version=nightly&amp;mode=debug&amp;edition=2024&amp;gist=6b7b341b8879bfdecb80ae72a8011a6d\" rel=\"nofollow\">compiles</a> today if we enable enough nightly features, but we expect Clippy<br>\nand Rust-Analyzer to enforce tag checks and provide first-class IDE support.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-rust notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"#[safety::requires( // 💡 define safety tags on an unsafe function\n    valid_ptr = &quot;src must be [valid](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/ptr/index.html#safety) for reads&quot;,\n    aligned = &quot;src must be properly aligned, even if T has size 0&quot;,\n    initialized = &quot;src must point to a properly initialized value of type T&quot;\n)]\npub unsafe fn read&lt;T&gt;(ptr: *const T) { }\n\nfn main() {\n    #[safety::checked( // 💡 discharge safety tags on an unsafe call\n        valid_ptr, aligned, initialized = &quot;optional reason&quot;\n    )]\n    unsafe { read(&amp;()) };\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c1\">#<span class=\"pl-kos\">[</span>safety<span class=\"pl-kos\">::</span>requires<span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span> <span class=\"pl-c\">// 💡 define safety tags on an unsafe function</span></span>\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">    valid_ptr = <span class=\"pl-s\">\"src must be [valid](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/ptr/index.html#safety) for reads\"</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">    aligned = <span class=\"pl-s\">\"src must be properly aligned, even if T has size 0\"</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">    initialized = <span class=\"pl-s\">\"src must point to a properly initialized value of type T\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"pl-c1\"><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">]</span></span>\n<span class=\"pl-k\">pub</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">unsafe</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">fn</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">read</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;</span><span class=\"pl-smi\">T</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">ptr</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">*</span><span class=\"pl-k\">const</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">T</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-k\">fn</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">main</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-c1\">#<span class=\"pl-kos\">[</span>safety<span class=\"pl-kos\">::</span>checked<span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span> <span class=\"pl-c\">// 💡 discharge safety tags on an unsafe call</span></span>\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">        valid_ptr<span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> aligned<span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> initialized = <span class=\"pl-s\">\"optional reason\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">    <span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">]</span></span>\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">unsafe</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">read</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">&amp;</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Artisan-Lab/rfcs/blob/safety-tags/text/0000-safety-tags.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3842",
            "title": "RFC: Safety Tags",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-13T17:31:21.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-07-31T14:48:26.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "zjp-CN",
                "url": "https://github.com/zjp-CN"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/517608?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This RFC extends the set of Unicode character which can be used in identifiers with <a href=\"https://util.unicode.org/UnicodeJsps/list-unicodeset.jsp?a=%5B%3AID_Compat_Math_Start%3DYes%3A%5D&amp;g=&amp;i=idtype\" rel=\"nofollow\">ID_Compat_Math_Start</a> and <a href=\"https://util.unicode.org/UnicodeJsps/list-unicodeset.jsp?a=%5B%3AID_Compat_Math_Continue%3DYes%3A%5D&amp;g=&amp;i=idtype\" rel=\"nofollow\">ID_Compat_Math_Continue</a>, most notable: ∇, ∂, ∞, subscripts ⁰¹²³⁴⁵⁶⁷⁸⁹⁺⁻⁼⁽⁾ and superscripts ₀₁₂₃₄₅₆₇₈₉₊₋₌₍₎.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This can be a boon to implementers of scientific concepts as they can write for example <code class=\"notranslate\">let ∇E₁₂ = 0.5;</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Danvil/rfcs/blob/compat_math_identifiers/text/3840-compat-math-identifiers.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3840",
            "title": "RFC: ID_Compat_Math characters allowed in identifiers",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-02T22:03:36.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-07-16T19:17:40.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Danvil",
                "url": "https://github.com/Danvil"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1295100?u=b0540abe14ddfb8c24578add2a8c960bc704a661&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Supercedes <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1241693645\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/issues/3268\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3268/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3268\">#3268</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Introduces a new attribute, <code class=\"notranslate\">#[rustc_scalable_vector(N)]</code>, which can be used to define new scalable vector types, such as those in Arm's Scalable Vector Extension (SVE), or RISC-V's Vector Extension (RVV).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">rustc_scalable_vector(N)</code> is internal compiler infrastructure that will be used only in the standard library to introduce scalable vector types which can then be stabilised. Only the infrastructure to define these types are introduced in this RFC, not the types or intrinsics that use it.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This RFC has a dependency on <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2662434146\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/issues/3729\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3729/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3729\">#3729</a> as scalable vectors are necessarily non-const <code class=\"notranslate\">Sized</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>There are some large unresolved questions in this RFC, the current purpose of the RFC is to indicate a intended direction for this work to justify an experimental implementation to help resolve those unresolved questions.</strong></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/davidtwco/rfcs/blob/repr-scalable/text/3838-scalable-vectors.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3838",
            "title": "`rustc_scalable_vector`",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-06T16:21:31.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-07-14T11:12:44.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "davidtwco",
                "url": "https://github.com/davidtwco"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12191912?u=4684c311c450833af74a06ef411bfe6af7ad207e&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This RFC proposes to add <code class=\"notranslate\">#[export_visibility = …]</code> attribute, which seems like a reasonable way to address the following issues:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1283517092\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/98449\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rust/issues/98449/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/98449\">rust-lang/rust#98449</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"649745016\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/73958\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rust/issues/73958/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/73958\">rust-lang/rust#73958</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This RFC complements the <code class=\"notranslate\">-Zdefault-visibility=...</code> command-line flag, which is tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2559002414\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/131090\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rust/issues/131090/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/131090\">rust-lang/rust#131090</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR replaces the Major Change Proposal (MCP) at <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3118462730\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/compiler-team/issues/881\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/compiler-team/issues/881/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/compiler-team/issues/881\">rust-lang/compiler-team#881</a><br>\n(/cc <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/bjorn3/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/bjorn3\">@bjorn3</a>, <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/ChrisDenton/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/ChrisDenton\">@ChrisDenton</a>, <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/chorman0773/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/chorman0773\">@chorman0773</a>, <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/joshtriplett/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/joshtriplett\">@joshtriplett</a>, <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/mati865/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/mati865\">@mati865</a>, <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/workingjubilee/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/workingjubilee\">@workingjubilee</a>, and <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/Urgau/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/Urgau\">@Urgau</a> who have kindly provided feedback in <a href=\"https://rust-lang.zulipchat.com/#narrow/stream/233931-xxx/topic/.60.23.5Bexport_visibility.20.3D.20.2E.2E.2E.5D.60.20attribute.20compiler-team.23881\" rel=\"nofollow\">the Zulip thread</a> associated with that MCP)</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">/cc <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/tmandry/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/tmandry\">@tmandry</a> from <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2861372907\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust-project-goals/issues/253\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rust-project-goals/issues/253/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust-project-goals/issues/253\">rust-lang/rust-project-goals#253</a>, because one area where this RFC seems needed is FFI tooling</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/anforowicz/rust-rfcs/blob/export-visibility/text/0000-export-visibility.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3834",
            "title": "RFC: `#[export_visibility = ...]` attribute.",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-11T23:43:20.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-16T19:34:28.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "anforowicz",
                "url": "https://github.com/anforowicz"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/154856872?u=549d98da76d371effb56d0d7f4dfcac951507814&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Proposal to add dedented string literals to Rust of the form: <code class=\"notranslate\">d\"string\"</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">With the following:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-rust notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"let sql = d&quot;\n    create table student(\n        id int primary key,\n        name text\n    )\n    &quot;;\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">let</span> sql = d\"\n    create table <span class=\"pl-en\">student</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span>\n        id int primary key<span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span>\n        name text\n    <span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span>\n    \"<span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Being equivalent to:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-rust notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"let sql = &quot;\\\ncreate table student(\n    id int primary key,\n    name text\n)&quot;;\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">let</span> sql = <span class=\"pl-s\">\"<span class=\"pl-cce\">\\</span></span>\n<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-cce\"></span>create table student(</span>\n<span class=\"pl-s\">    id int primary key,</span>\n<span class=\"pl-s\">    name text</span>\n<span class=\"pl-s\">)\"</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/nik-contrib/rfcs/blob/dedented_strings/text/3830-dedented-string-literals.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3830",
            "title": "RFC: Dedented String Literals",
            "date_modified": "2025-06-20T18:36:58.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-05T15:40:28.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "nik-rev",
                "url": "https://github.com/nik-rev"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48135649?u=f47185e959d8ac7ec628af62c40ed782e9d6485b&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Noratrieb/rfcs/blob/ununsize_locals/text/1909-unsized-rvalues.md\">Original RFC</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Noratrieb/rfcs/blob/ununsize_locals/text/3829-de-rfc-unsized-locals.md\">New RFC</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Noratrieb/rfcs/blob/ununsize_locals/text/3829-de-rfc-unsized-locals.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3829",
