        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191960014?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">See discussion on internals <a href=\"https://internals.rust-lang.org/t/pre-rfc-allow-procedural-macros-to-be-placed-in-the-same-crate-package-as-app/23005\" rel=\"nofollow\">here</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I feel the need to clarify that this is not about crates, but packages. I had them confused the initial time I wrote the document.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/ora-0/rust-rfcs/blob/master/text/3778-proc-macro-in-same-package-as-app.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3826",
            "title": "RFC: Procedural macros in same package as app",
            "date_modified": "2025-06-12T02:20:20.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-05-30T07:45:15.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "ora-0",
                "url": "https://github.com/ora-0"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60879563?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This proposal was initially shared in a <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/rust/comments/1kwud96/proposal_to_reconcile_generics_and_rusts_orphan/?utm_source=share&amp;utm_medium=web3x&amp;utm_name=web3xcss&amp;utm_term=1&amp;utm_content=share_button\" rel=\"nofollow\">Reddit post</a> I authored to introduce the idea and gather community feedback:</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">“Proposal to reconcile generics and Rust’s orphan rule”</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">While the post is still recent and awaiting responses, it serves as an early exposition of the problem and the motivation behind this RFC.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/victorGhiglione/rfcs/blob/local_trait_restriction_for_orphan_rule/text/3773-local-type-filter.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3821",
            "title": "RFC: Allow generic impls using local trait bounds",
            "date_modified": "2025-06-07T16:26:58.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-05-27T19:39:12.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "victorGhiglione",
                "url": "https://github.com/victorGhiglione"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1896483?u=c6fc0bdfda0b94322521aecdf211fabe16d2edea&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">tldr: make it easier/safer to use <code class=\"notranslate\">target_feature</code> in traits.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Also see prior discussion in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2972360895\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/139368\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rust/issues/139368/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/139368\">rust-lang/rust#139368</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/veluca93/rfcs/blob/tft/text/3820-target-feature-traits.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3820",
            "title": "RFC: Changes to `target_feature` attribute",
            "date_modified": "2025-06-22T22:39:29.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-05-25T19:25:50.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "veluca93",
                "url": "https://github.com/veluca93"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/84762?u=65f5941f516bf6a9c5be4be8dce0aadebb37690e&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This RFC describes an Extended Standard Library (ESL) for Rust.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Please see <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NzuF8QVVi9wcmvmHa1_-hwRLNb9UoxWNbUcdOsqWJyc/edit?usp=sharing\" rel=\"nofollow\">this document</a> for additional information about fundraising.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I’d like to thank Dirkjan Ochtman (<a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/djc/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/djc\">@djc</a>), Adolfo Ochagavía (<a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/aochagavia/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/aochagavia\">@aochagavia</a>), Alex Gaynor (<a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/alex/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/alex\">@alex</a>), James Munns (OneVariable GmbH, <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/jamesmunns/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/jamesmunns\">@jamesmunns</a>), Andrew Gallant (<a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/BurntSushi/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/BurntSushi\">@BurntSushi</a>), Marco Ieni (<a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/marcoieni/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/marcoieni\">@marcoieni</a>), and many others for their feedback and assistance while working on this. My thanks does not necessarily imply their endorsement.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/bdaehlie/rust-rfcs/blob/extended-standard-library/text/0000-extended-standard-library.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
